+## `bin/clean-workspaces.sh`
+
+Removes stale build workspaces: every directory directly under the workspace root whose
+newest file is more than N days old. Requires Bash and GNU `find`.
+
+```
+bin/clean-workspaces.sh [--root DIR] [--days N] [--dry-run]
+```
+
+| Option | Default | Meaning |
+|---|---|---|
+| `-r`, `--root DIR` | `workspaces` | Workspace root (relative paths resolve from the current directory) |
+| `-d`, `--days N` | `7` | Age threshold in days (non-negative integer) |
+| `-n`, `--dry-run` | off | List what would be removed (`would remove <name> (age Nd)`) and remove nothing |
+| `-h`, `--help` | | Show usage |
+
+Examples:
+
+```
+bin/clean-workspaces.sh --dry-run
+bin/clean-workspaces.sh --root /srv/ci/workspaces --days 14
+```
+
+Exit status: `0` on success, `64` for bad arguments, `66` if the root is not a directory.
+Symlinks under the root are not followed, and `/` is refused as a root. Run with
+`--dry-run` first when pointing it at a new location.
